{"Title":"An Act designating a portion of state highway Route 7 in the town of Sheffield as the Brigadier-General John G. Barnard highway\r\n","BillNumber":"S2940","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"S29","Name":"Senate Committee on Rules","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S29","ResponseDate":"2024-08-15T19:09:06.667"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2940/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Amendment","Pinslip":"Senate, August 16, 2024 - The committee on Rules to whom was referred House Bill designating a portion of state highway Route 7 in the town of Sheffield as the Brigadier-General John G. Barnard highway (House, No. 4617); reports, recommending that the same ought to pass with an amendment striking out all after the enacting clause and inserting in place thereof the text of Senate document numbered 2940.","DocumentText":"\tThe portion of United State highway route 7 in the town of Sheffield beginning at mile marker 4.9  in the town of Sheffield and ending at mile marker 5.7  shall be designated and known as the Brigadier-General John G. Barnard highway in honor of Brigadier-General John G. Barnard for his dedicated service in the United States Army as Chief Engineer of the Civil War Defenses of Washington. The Massachusetts Department of Transportation shall erect  and maintain suitable  markers along the portion of United States highway route 7 bearing the designation in compliance with the standards of the department.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}